 running mixed workloads\n- More granular control over scheduling\n\n## When to Use Mode 4\n\nThis is where I need to be honest about my uncertainty. The CCS mode values and their exact semantics have changed across driver versions, and I'm not confident about the precise definition of **mode 4** specifically.\n\nI'd recommend checking:\n- **`xe` driver documentation** in your kernel source (`drivers/gpu/driver/xe/`)\n- The module parameter definition itself, typically found in `xe_drv.c` or similar, where the enum values are documented inline\n- Recent Intel Arc community discussions, since these tuning options evolve with driver updates\n\n## Practical Note\n\nFor most single-GPU users, **CCS mode rarely matters** for everyday performance. The differences become more relevant in:\n- Multi-GPU configurations\n- Specific compute-heavy or copy-heavy workloads\n- Benchmarking/tuning scenarios\n\nWould you like me to help you find the exact documentation in your specific driver version? If you can share your driver/kernel version, that would help narrow down the precise semantics."}